From: polaris port <local@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: panel: Enable prepare_prev_first flag for NT35596s

This panel needs DSI commands sent in its prepare() callback, so the
panel's prepare must run after the DSI host has been powered on
(pre_enable).  Without prepare_prev_first, the DRM bridge chain runs the
panel's prepare() before the DSI host power_on, so the first
mipi_dsi_dcs_write() reaches dsi_host_transfer() with
msm_host->power_on == false and returns -EINVAL:

  panel-jdi-nt35596s ae94000.dsi.0: failed to send DCS Init 1st Code: -22

Set the prepare_prev_first flag to run the panel prepare at the end of
the pre_enable chain (after host power_on), allowing the DCS init
commands to be transmitted.  This is the same flag already set for the
other SDM845 panels (sofef00, s6e3fc2x01, nt36672a, ft8719).

Adapted from Icenowy Zheng's sdm845-mainline commit 2c875e90
("drm: panel: Enable prepare_prev_first flag for NT35596s"), which is
part of MR !85 "Hotfixes for sdm845-xiaomi-polaris" that has not yet
been merged into the 7.1 branch.

Tested on Xiaomi Mi MIX 2S (polaris, SDM845): with this and the DSI PLL
digital-top fix, the panel receives its init sequence and the display
outputs.

Signed-off-by: polaris port <local@localhost>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt35596s.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt35596s.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt35596s.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt35596s.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt35596s.c
@@ -477,6 +477,7 @@ static int nt35596s_panel_add(struct nt35596s_panel *pinfo)
 
 	drm_panel_init(&pinfo->base, dev, &panel_funcs, DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DSI);
 
+	pinfo->base.prepare_prev_first = true;
 	drm_panel_add(&pinfo->base);
 
 	return 0;
-- 
